>> Version 1.0.0.0

Diffie-Hellman uses module arithmatic combined with exponents to enable two remote parties to agree a secret.

It works on the premis that stacking multiple exponents is the same this as multiplying the exponents.

That is to say that 
    
    2 ^ 3 ^ 2    =     2 ^ (3 x 2)
    2 ^ 3 ^ 2 = 64
    2 ^ (3 x 2) = 64

So 

    3 ^ ($Key1 x  $Key2)     =     3 ^ ($Key2 x  $Key1)

So the first step of the exchange is for each party to add an exponent

    3 ^ ($Key1)         #person 1  
    3 ^ ($Key2)         #person 2

The users then swap and add their exponent to end up with 

    3 ^ ($Key2 x $Key1)         #person 1  
    3 ^ ($Key1 x $Key2)         #person 2

The problem though is that while both parties will get the same output, the equasions are human readable.
To get arround this problem we will make some small adjustments.

We will start by picking two prime number _G snd _N. 
_N must be bigger thamn _G.

Now instead of exchanging the _G ^ ($Key1) we will preform _G ^ ($Key1) mod _N and return the output
appebding the mod _N operation in this manner obsures the value of $Key1.

so we end up with 

    _G ^ (($Key1) mod _N) ^ ($Key2) mod _N)    =    _G ^ (($Key2) mod _N) ^ ($Key1) mod _N
